2026-10-16T15:25:27.9038483Z   ISSUE_NUMBER: 56119
2026-10-16T15:25:27.9038697Z   ISSUE_TITLE: fix(core): fresh standalone run rejects a model before catalog refresh completes
2026-10-16T15:25:27.9049995Z   ISSUE_BODY: ## Description

Fresh-state standalone runs reject a live model while the initial catalog refresh is pending.

## Summary

A fresh `run --standalone --model opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free` can fail with `provider.no-route` while the startup catalog request is still pending. The bundled catalog lacks this live model. Delaying only that request reproduces the failure; a fresh run against the normal endpoint returned `OK`.

## OpenCode version

Latest npm `@opencode/cli`: 2.0.31, installed in an isolated prefix. Source inspected: release tag `v2.0.31` and current `dev` at `ed772f5009755b5262805a7ba07e66e1417f140a`; the relevant catalog and model-resolution paths match. Runtime reproduction used the published binary, not a source build.

## Plugins

No user plugins or credentials; fresh HOME/XDG roots and project config disabled.

## Steps to reproduce

Install the stated release into a temporary prefix, set `OC` to its `opencode` executable, and run this Python script. It serves an unchanged copy of the current catalog with a three-second response delay using the supported process-level URL override. It uses fresh state, runs no tools, and removes its temporary state. Requires Python 3 and curl.

```sh
W=$(mktemp -d)
npm install --prefix "$W/oc" @opencode/cli@2.0.31
export OC="$W/oc/node_modules/.bin/opencode"
export TMPDIR="$W"
# Save the following Python as repro.py, then run: python3 repro.py
```

```python
import http.server, json, os, pathlib, subprocess, tempfile, threading, time

binary = pathlib.Path(os.environ["OC"]).resolve()
body = subprocess.check_output(["curl", "-fsSL", "https://models.opencode.ai/api.json"])
assert "glm-5.3-flash-free" in json.loads(body)["opencode"]["models"]
work = pathlib.Path(tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix="opencode-catalog-", dir=os.environ["TMPDIR"]))

class Catalog(http.server.BaseHTTPRequestHandler):
    def do_GET(self):
        time.sleep(3)
        try:
            self.send_response(200)
            self.end_headers()
            self.wfile.write(body)
        except (BrokenPipeError, ConnectionResetError):
            pass
    def log_message(self, *args):
        pass

server = http.server.ThreadingHTTPServer(("127.0.0.1", 0), Catalog)
threading.Thread(target=server.serve_forever, daemon=True).start()
env = {"PATH": os.environ["PATH"], "HOME": str(work), "OPENCODE_DISABLE_PROJECT_CONFIG": "1"}
for name, suffix in [("CONFIG", ".config"), ("DATA", ".local/share"), ("CACHE", ".cache"), ("STATE", ".local/state")]:
    env["XDG_" + name + "_HOME"] = str(work / suffix)
env["OPENCODE_MODELS_URL"] = "http://127.0.0.1:" + str(server.server_port)
try:
    result = subprocess.run([str(binary), "run", "--standalone", "--format", "json", "--title", "Catalog probe", "--model", "opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free", "Reply exactly OK. Do not use tools."], cwd=work, env=env, stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=30)
    print("exit:", result.returncode)
    for line in result.stdout.splitlines():
        event = json.loads(line)
        if event.get("type") == "error":
            print(json.dumps(event["error"]))
finally:
    server.shutdown()
    server.server_close()
    import shutil
    shutil.rmtree(work)

```

## Expected behavior

A valid explicitly selected model should resolve once the in-flight initial catalog fetch supplies it, rather than be reported as unavailable solely because it is absent from the bundled floor. This need not delay runs for models already present. The documented one-command standalone CI workflow has no warm-up prerequisite.

## Actual behavior

The delayed-catalog probe failed in three of three fresh homes. The self-contained script above also reproduced it in a fourth fresh home:

```text
exit: 1
{"type": "provider.no-route", "message": "Model unavailable: opencode/glm-5.3-flash-free"}
```

A fresh run against the normal endpoint returned `OK` and exit 0. With the delayed endpoint, a private server’s model list changed from missing the ID to listing it after the response completed. The subsequent standalone request produced no output within 35 seconds and was stopped; this verifies catalog refresh, not a successful warmed request.

## Evidence

- Expected source: [CLI command documentation](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/ed772f5009755b5262805a7ba07e66e1417f140a/services/www/src/docs/content/cli/commands.mdx) documents standalone CI runs with an explicit model; the reproduction's fetched catalog contains the selected ID.
- Failure source: The published binary's four fresh-state failures above, with only the catalog response delayed locally.
- Evidence provenance: observed
- Local verification: reproduced
- Reproduction completeness: complete

[Catalog startup](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/ed772f5009755b5262805a7ba07e66e1417f140a/packages/core/src/models-dev.ts#L386-L434) can serve the bundled snapshot while the initial refresh runs in the background; [explicit model resolution](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/ed772f5009755b5262805a7ba07e66e1417f140a/packages/core/src/session/runner/model.ts#L75-L90) rejects a missing ID without waiting for that fetch or refreshing and retrying. The release bundle lacks this model; the current default-branch snapshot already includes it, but the startup/resolution paths remain unchanged. Current source was inspected, not executed.

Related: [#50011](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/50011) refreshes release snapshots; [#50012](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/pull/50012) fixes a missed notification after refresh. This reproduction concerns failure while the fetch is still pending. [#34837](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/34837) requested fresh focused reports after lifecycle changes; [#36117](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/issues/36117) concerns early partial catalog reads.

## Restoration check

With a model absent from the bundle but present in a successful delayed catalog response, the first fresh standalone run should resolve that model and produce the requested reply. A model absent from both catalogs should still fail meaningfully; a bundled model should remain usable without requiring a successful network refresh.

## Operating System

macOS, Darwin 27.0.0, arm64.

## Terminal

Noninteractive subprocess with stdin closed.

## Triage assessment

- Impact level: P2
- Assessment status: supported
- Impact basis: A valid first command fails in fresh state when the catalog fetch loses the startup race. This affects newly added models absent from the bundle; the measured delay fixture failed consistently, while the live-endpoint control succeeded. Population frequency is unknown.
- Workaround status: unverified
- Workaround basis: Polling a private server until the model appears restored catalog visibility, but the local warmed request timed out. Earlier supplied incident notes report success after warm-up; that full procedure was not verified on this release.

